From: Liuqin Linux Kit maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: complete the SM8475 USB SerDes table

The Liuqin downstream 4 nm sequence programs VCO_TUNE2_MODE1,
CORE_CLK_EN and CMN_CONFIG_1, but the imported USB table omitted all three.
Add the missing writes before PHY reset release and SerDes start. Use the
V6 COM names matching the actual offsets instead of unrelated V5 names;
all other address/value pairs stay unchanged. TX/RX, PCS, orientation,
role policy and the board's Gen1 limit are unchanged.

Reference: MiCode Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e,
arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/liuqin-sm8475.dtsi usb_qmp_dp_phy;
also present in OS2.0.6.0.VMYCNXM dtbo.img entry 15.

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -1100,55 +1100,60 @@
 };
 
